text: |-
  Utah State Bar:
  @BasedSamParker
  @SamParkerSenate
  Gov. Spencer Cox appoints
  Tony F. Graf to the Fourth
  District Court
  Press Releases
  Friday, May 2, 2025
  PRESS RELEASE
  SALT LAKE CITY (May 2, 2025) - Utah Gov. Spencer J. Cox has
  appointed Tony F. Graf to the Fourth District Court, filling a vacancy left
  by the retirement of Judge Robert Lunnen. Judicial appointments are
  subject to confirmation by the Utah Senate.
  "Tony Graf brings a steady hand, strong ethics, and the kind of judgment
  we count on in Utah's judiciary," said Gov. Cox. "From prosecuting
  difficult cases to training new attorneys — his experience reflects a
  commitment to justice and public service."
  Graf currently serves as a Deputy County Attorney for Davis County,
  where he prosecutes physical and sexual abuse cases. He previously led
  the Special Victims Unit for the Utah County Attorney's Office and served
  as a Deputy District Attorney in Salt Lake County. His diverse experience
  also includes roles as an Assistant Attorney General in American
  Samoa, Deputy District Attorney in Lincoln County, Nevada, and Special
  Assistant United States Attorney in Washington, D.C.
